      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_conchonius_en/",
      "html": "<p>Wild-collected rosy barbs, originating from the vicinity of Calcutta (the type locality of Barbus conchonius), look completely different from the aquarium strains. Males of the wild fish become metallic black and get a red caudal peduncle. Each scale is ornamented with a bright silver spot.</p><p>The aquarium strains of the rosy barb apparently do not belong to the species Barbus conchonius at all.</p><p>Keeping wild-collected rosy barbs is no different from keeping the domesticated ones. They are hardy fish and very easy to keep.</p><p>Barbus: Latin, meaning \"the bearded one\", referring to the barbels. conchonius: after the common name of the fish in Bengal.</p>"
    }
  ],
